{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3060","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3060","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3060\",\"parent_revision\":\"8a66e2fb5b3498948df0d6fd85221b0cb6780d9a\",\"root_revision\":\"13acbe51317903b175f86c4359bb9e4ebe2a3aeda819ffd6d3f1a5f01d1b5f8a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe runtime strings that tell an agent what to call next steer it away from paginated navigation. The compact response's hint recommends loading full content as its first suggestion. The over-budget response tells a caller to request sections individually \u2014 advice a caller who already narrowed to one oversized section has exhausted. Neither mentions the paginated navigation parameters.\\n\\nAgents follow these strings. Documentation is a weaker lever: these are read on every call, at the moment of the decision.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:11:07.292876Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: runtime hints steer agents away from paginated navigation\\nDate: 2026-08-20\\nGoal: Make _build_compact_manifest()'s _hint and _build_over_budget_view()'s _usage in backlog_core/server.py comply with R7 (Hints must be actionable) in agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md.\\nConditions:\\n1. Exact current text/location of the two violating hint strings | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. R7 requirement text and its three prohibitions | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Existing in-package pattern for a paginated-navigation hint (disclosure_handler.py next_call) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Whether the over-budget call site has access to \\\"caller already narrowed to one section\\\" signal | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Whether disclosure_handler.py itself needs changes vs. server.py only | Status: DERIVABLE (confirm during Impact Radius)\\n6. Existing test conventions for backlog_core/server.py hint-construction functions | Status: DERIVABLE (confirm during Impact Radius / Files)\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:13:57.868084Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n\\n**Rationale**: Code in two functions violates R7 (normative requirement in agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md) by generating hints that recommend actions agents have already exhausted or actions the response cannot support.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Direct source verification against normative requirement R7. Compared violating code against correct reference implementation in disclosure_handler.py and container-level requirement text.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: backlog_view(summary=True) and over-budget backlog_view() responses \u2192 agent receives hint recommending full-content retrieval as first action (summary=False) or pagination actions (navigate=, skip_tokens=) not demonstrated in the response object itself.\\n\\n**Evidence Chain**:\\n- Violating location 1: server.py:2306-2309 (_build_compact_manifest._hint) recommends \\\"Load full content: summary=False\\\" first, violating R7 clause \\\"never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion\\\"\\n- Violating location 2: server.py:2379-2387 (_build_over_budget_view._usage) recommends \\\"request them individually\\\" without naming pagination parameters (navigate=, head=, skip_tokens=) that exist in the response sections_index but are absent from the hint itself, violating R7 clause \\\"never name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies\\\"\\n- Correct pattern reference: disclosure_handler.py:487-490 (next_call hint) demonstrates the required form \u2014 hint uses navigate= and skip_tokens= parameters documented in the same node's bounded content structure\\n- Requirement source: agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164, R7 normative requirement\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:14:32.531697Z</sub>\\n\\n## Wave 0 Technical Research \u2014 hint-construction convention\\n\\n### Established pattern: `next_call`\\n\\nThree call sites in `backlog_core/` and `sam_schema/` build a machine-actionable continuation\\nhint under the literal key `next_call`. All three share the same shape:\\n\\n1. **`backlog_core/disclosure_handler.py` `_handle_extract()` (around line 484-490)** \u2014 the\\n   pattern the item's context already cites as canonical:\\n   ```python\\n   next_call: str | None = None\\n   if bounded.truncated:\\n       next_skip = skip_tokens + bounded.returned_tokens\\n       next_call = (\\n           f'backlog_view(selector=\\\"{selector}\\\", navigate=\\\"{ordinal}\\\", '\\n           f\\\"head={head_tokens}, skip_tokens={next_skip})\\\"\\n       )\\n   ```\\n2. **`backlog_core/server.py` `backlog_list()` (around line 2267-2268)**:\\n   ```python\\n   if has_more:\\n       response[\\\"next_call\\\"] = f\\\"backlog_list(offset={offset + effective_limit}, limit={effective_limit})\\\"\\n   ```\\n3. **`sam_schema/server.py` `_paginate_results()` (around line 175-177)**, a shared helper used\\n   by both `sam_plan` and `sam_task` list/ready actions:\\n   ```python\\n   if has_more:\\n       next_offset = offset + len(page)\\n       result.next_call = f\\\"{tool_name}(offset={next_offset}, limit={effective_limit})\\\"\\n   ```\\n\\nCommon shape across all three (this is the convention a fix must match):\\n\\n- **Field name**: `next_call`, always a bare string (or `None`/absent), never nested under a\\n  prose paragraph.\\n- **Conditional, not unconditional**: the field is populated only when a next step is genuinely\\n  actionable (`bounded.truncated`, `has_more`). When there is nothing left to fetch, the field is\\n  omitted/`None` \u2014 the hint never recommends an action the caller has already exhausted (this is\\n  literally R7's second clause).\\n- **Content is a literal, copy-pasteable call expression**: `tool_name(param=value, ...)`, not a\\n  sentence describing what to do. The reader can paste it directly.\\n- **Parameters cite exactly the current response's state**: the *cumulative* position is computed\\n  from values already in scope at the call site \u2014 `skip_tokens + bounded.returned_tokens`,\\n  `offset + effective_limit`, `offset + len(page)` \u2014 not a static default. The caller never has to\\n  compute the next offset itself.\\n- **One suggestion, not several**: each of the three sites emits exactly one `next_call` string,\\n  matching R7's \\\"never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion\\\" \u2014 there is no\\n  competing alternative offered.\\n\\n### The two violating call sites do not follow this convention\\n\\n`_build_compact_manifest()` (`backlog_core/server.py` around 2275-2314) and\\n`_build_over_budget_view()` (around 2352-2392) both diverge from every element of the pattern\\nabove:\\n\\n- Different field names (`_hint`, `_usage`) instead of `next_call`.\\n- Content is prose containing two-to-three alternative calls as literal strings embedded in a\\n  multi-line human-readable message, not a single machine-actionable expression.\\n- Unconditional: both functions always populate the field on every call, regardless of what the\\n  caller has already requested. `_build_compact_manifest`'s `_hint` recommends \\\"Load full content\\\"\\n  as its *first* line unconditionally \u2014 this is the literal violation of R7's first clause (\\\"must\\n  never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion\\\").\\n- No use of already-known caller state: at the `_build_over_budget_view` call site\\n  (`server.py` around line 2681, inside the `if not summary:` branch), `sections_filter` (set at\\n  line 2633 from the `sections` param) and `section` (the raw param) are both in scope and\\n  non-None whenever the caller already narrowed the request \u2014 but neither is passed into\\n  `_build_over_budget_view`, so the returned `_usage` string always suggests `sections=`/`section=`\\n  usage even to a caller who is already using it. This is the literal violation of R7's second\\n  clause (\\\"must never recommend an action the caller has already exhausted\\\").\\n\\n### R7 normative text (`docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`, \\\"R7 \u2014 Hints must be\\nactionable\\\")\\n\\n> A response that withholds content states what the caller must do to obtain it, using addresses\\n> valid in that same response. A hint must never recommend retrieving everything as its first\\n> suggestion, never recommend an action the caller has already exhausted, and never name a\\n> mechanism absent from the response it accompanies.\\n\\nR6 (same doc) explicitly cross-references R7's hint as the mechanism for reaching paginated\\ncontent: \\\"the caller reaches the remainder with a same-tool page request named by R7's hint.\\\"\\n\\n### Prior art: no ADR governs hint *string construction* specifically\\n\\nNo ADR or PR title matching \\\"hint\\\" was found scoped to the construction convention itself \u2014 R7 in\\nthe consumption contract doc is the only normative spec, and the `next_call` pattern above is\\nimplicit convention (established by the three working call sites and their tests), not\\ndocumented separately. The fix should express its `next_call` construction convention inline in\\ncode (docstring/comment), consistent with how `_handle_extract()` already documents its own\\n`next_call` semantics.\\n\\n### Existing test coverage (prior art for what a fix's tests must add)\\n\\n`tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` already asserts *fidelity* (the hint embeds the caller's exact\\nselector) for both violating sites, but not R7 compliance:\\n\\n- `test_backlog_view_summary_true_hint_contains_selector` (around line 1046) \u2014 asserts `_hint`\\n  contains the exact selector string, nothing about suggestion ordering.\\n- `test_build_over_budget_view_usage_mentions_sections_param` (around line 3898) \u2014 asserts `_usage`\\n  contains `sections=` and the selector, nothing about conditioning on prior narrowing.\\n\\nNeither existing test would catch the R7 violations described above (first-suggestion ordering,\\nalready-exhausted advice) \u2014 a fix needs new tests asserting: (1) `_hint`'s first suggestion is\\nsection-scoped when `sections_index` is present, not full-content load, and (2) `_usage`/an\\nequivalent field omits or reorders the sections-narrowing suggestion when the caller already\\nsupplied `section`/`sections`.\\n\\n### Recurrence assessment\\n\\nConfirmed two call sites need the fix (`_build_compact_manifest`, `_build_over_budget_view`); no\\nthird violating site exists \u2014 every other hint-construction call site in `backlog_core/` and\\n`sam_schema/` (`backlog_list`, `_handle_extract`, `_paginate_results`) already follows the\\n`next_call` convention correctly.\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] No hint recommends retrieving everything as its first suggestion, per R7\\n- [ ] The over-budget hint offers an action a narrowed caller has not already taken\\n- [ ] Hints name only mechanisms present in the response they accompany\\n- [ ] Addresses appearing in a hint are valid in that same response\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1 \u2014 small change, disproportionate effect on agent behaviour\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d51fd2ac542e328f570c192a126c6df3c76b1e37d3d4b341e932288a708faecf\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPx23cg\"}"}